{# @locked whole #}
{%- set banned_block = "" %}
{%- if banned_words %}
{%- set bw_lines = ["", "BANNED WORDS: never use these or close variations:"] %}
{%- for w in banned_words %}
{%- set _ = bw_lines.append('  ✗ "' ~ w ~ '"') %}
{%- endfor %}
{%- set _ = bw_lines.append("") %}
{%- set banned_block = bw_lines | join("\n") %}
{%- endif %}

{{ language_instruction }}

{{ brand_context }}

A brand made one social picture. Plan 3 new pictures that carry the same message, each from a clearly different angle: a different
choice of what to lead with, shown as a different scene and a different look. They are fresh takes, not small variations of the
same picture.

Angle 1 (Contrarian): lead with what most people get wrong about this.
Angle 2 (The why): lead with the belief or reason behind the message, shown as a scene a viewer recognises.
Angle 3 (Concrete outcome): lead with the specific result the source gives, using only real details from it.

For each picture write:
- headline: the words printed on the picture, at most 10 words, in the brand voice. Only facts from the source, never an invented number.
- scene: what the image model should draw behind the headline, in 1 to 3 plain sentences. Describe subject, setting, light and
  composition. No words, letters, logos or text in the scene itself, and no real person's name or face.
- look: exactly one id from the list below. Use a different look for each picture where it suits the message.

LOOKS (id: what it looks like):
{% for id, words in looks %}
- {{ id }}: {{ words }}
{% endfor %}

The original picture's look was "{{ current_look }}" and its scene was:
{{ source_scene | untrusted("source_scene") }}

Never use em dashes anywhere in the output.
{{ language_instruction }}
{{ banned_block }}
THE PICTURE'S WORDS (headline, slide text, description):
{{ content | untrusted("source_content") }}

Return valid JSON only:
{
  "angles": [
    {"name": "Contrarian", "rationale": "one sentence on why this framing works here", "headline": "...", "scene": "...", "look": "one id from the list"},
    {"name": "The why", "rationale": "...", "headline": "...", "scene": "...", "look": "..."},
    {"name": "Concrete outcome", "rationale": "...", "headline": "...", "scene": "...", "look": "..."}
  ]
}
{# @end #}
